{
  "id": "8ce32a02-4919-458f-b01d-afbac391fe3c",
  "page_title": "'Using your data with Azure OpenAI securely'",
  "page_description": "Use this article to learn about securely using your data for text generation in Azure OpenAI.",
  "page_date": "07/15/2024",
  "chunk_title": "Configure Storage Account",
  "chunk_content": "Configure Storage Account  ### Enable trusted service  To allow access to your Storage Account from Azure OpenAI and Azure AI Search, you need to set up Storage Account to bypass your Azure OpenAI and Azure AI Search as trusted services based on managed identity.  In the Azure portal, navigate to your storage account networking tab, choose \"Selected networks\", and then select Allow Azure services on the trusted services list to access this storage account and click Save.  ### Disable public network access  You can disable public network access of your Storage Account in the Azure portal.   To allow access to your Storage Account from your client machines, like using Azure OpenAI Studio, you need to create private endpoint connections that connect to your blob storage.",
